slurm-monitor: configurable token audience

- OAuthSettings.audience (env SLURM_MONITOR_OAUTH_AUDIENCE, comma-separated,
  default "account") replaces the hard-coded audience="account" in
  verify_token. "account" is what Keycloak puts in tokens of clients that set
  no audience, so a user's sign-in token for any client in the realm was
  accepted. The stack sets "slurm-monitor": Waldur exchanges the user's token
  for one issued for slurm-monitor before calling it.
- tests/slurm_monitor/api/test_token_audience.py covers the default, a
  configured list and the environment variable.

